{
  "title": "Stage 2: Counting",
  "summary": "Count status codes with CountBy and rank the busiest endpoints with GroupBy, OrderByDescending and Take.",
  "minutes": 14,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Briefing: counting things",
      "body": [
        "The first questions anyone asks of a log are *how many*. How many 500s? Which endpoints are busiest?",
        "",
        "For \"how many of each\", .NET 9 added `CountBy`. It returns one `KeyValuePair` per distinct key, with the count as the `Value`:",
        "",
        "```csharp fragment",
        "foreach (var (status, count) in entries.CountBy(e => e.Status).OrderBy(p => p.Key))",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"{status}: {count}\");",
        "```",
        "",
        "It is a shortcut for the `GroupBy` you already know. When you want more than a count per group, reach for `GroupBy`:",
        "",
        "```csharp fragment",
        "entries.GroupBy(e => e.Endpoint)",
        "    .Select(g => new { Endpoint = g.Key, Hits = g.Count() })",
        "    .OrderByDescending(x => x.Hits)",
        "    .ThenBy(x => x.Endpoint)          // ties: alphabetical, so output is stable",
        "    .Take(3);",
        "```",
        "",
        "From this stage on the program stops printing every entry and keeps the `Parsed:` line."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "var codes = new[] { 200, 404, 200, 500, 200, 404 };",
        "",
        "foreach (var (code, count) in codes.CountBy(c => c).OrderByDescending(p => p.Value))",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"{code} x{count}\");"
      ],
      "answer": [
        "200 x3",
        "404 x2",
        "500 x1"
      ],
      "explain": "`CountBy` counts each distinct value: 200 three times, 404 twice, 500 once. `OrderByDescending(p => p.Value)` puts the biggest count first."
    },
    {
      "type": "order",
      "prompt": "Arrange the query for the three busiest endpoints, busiest first, ties alphabetically.",
      "lines": [
        "var top = entries",
        "    .GroupBy(e => e.Endpoint)",
        "    .Select(g => new { Endpoint = g.Key, Hits = g.Count() })",
        "    .OrderByDescending(x => x.Hits)",
        "    .ThenBy(x => x.Endpoint)",
        "    .Take(3);"
      ],
      "explain": "Group, summarise, sort by the main key, break ties, then cut. `Take` before sorting would take three arbitrary endpoints."
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "Why add `.ThenBy(x => x.Endpoint)` when the task only asks for the busiest endpoints?",
      "options": [
        "So endpoints with the same number of hits always come out in the same order",
        "Because `OrderByDescending` cannot be followed by `Take` otherwise",
        "To remove duplicate endpoints",
        "It makes the sort faster"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "Without a tie-breaker the order of equal items depends on the input order. Output you test, diff or show in a dashboard should be deterministic."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Status codes and busy endpoints",
      "carry": true,
      "prompt": [
        "Replace the entry listing with two summaries.",
        "",
        "1. Stop printing each entry; keep the `Parsed:` line.",
        "2. Print an empty line, `Status codes:`, then `code: count` for every status, lowest code first. Use `CountBy`.",
        "3. Print an empty line, `Top endpoints:`, then the three endpoints (method and path) with the most requests as `endpoint: hits`, most first, ties alphabetically.",
        "",
        "For this input:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "2026-03-04T09:00:00 10.0.0.1 GET /api/orders 200 110ms",
        "2026-03-04T09:00:20 10.0.0.1 GET /api/orders/7 200 45ms",
        "2026-03-04T09:01:00 10.0.0.2 GET /api/search 200 320ms",
        "2026-03-04T09:02:30 10.0.0.1 POST /api/orders 201 180ms",
        "2026-03-04T09:05:00 10.0.0.3 GET /health 200 2ms",
        "2026-03-04T09:10:00 10.0.0.2 GET /api/search 200 410ms",
        "not a log line",
        "2026-03-04T09:45:00 10.0.0.1 GET /api/orders 200 130ms",
        "2026-03-04T09:46:10 10.0.0.2 GET /api/search 500 2300ms",
        "2026-03-04T09:46:15 10.0.0.4 GET /api/search 500 2100ms",
        "2026-03-04T09:46:40 10.0.0.2 GET /api/search 200 390ms",
        "2026-03-04T09:47:00 10.0.0.4 POST /api/orders 503 30ms",
        "2026-03-04T09:50:00 10.0.0.3 GET /health 200 3ms",
        "2026-03-04T09:52:00 10.0.0.1 GET /api/orders/7 404 12ms",
        "2026-03-04T10:30:00 10.0.0.3 GET /health 200 2ms",
        "2026-03-04T10:31:00 10.0.0.1 GET /api/orders 200 105ms",
        "2026-03-04T10:31:30 10.0.0.2 GET /api/search 200 350ms",
        "2026-03-04 10:32:00 10.0.0.2 GET /api/search 200 350ms",
        "2026-03-04T09:40:00 10.0.0.4 GET /api/search 200 15ms",
        "2026-03-04T10:33:00 10.0.0.4 GET /api/search 200 18ms",
        "```",
        "",
        "print exactly:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "Parsed: 18, skipped: 2",
        "",
        "Status codes:",
        "200: 13",
        "201: 1",
        "404: 1",
        "500: 2",
        "503: 1",
        "",
        "Top endpoints:",
        "GET /api/search: 8",
        "GET /api/orders: 3",
        "GET /health: 3",
        "```"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "using System.Globalization;",
        "",
        "var lines = new List<string>();",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "    lines.Add(line);",
        "",
        "var candidates = lines.Where(l => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(l)).ToList();",
        "",
        "var entries = candidates",
        "    .Select(TryParseEntry)",
        "    .OfType<Entry>()",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "foreach (var e in entries)",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"{e.Time:HH:mm:ss} {e.Ip} {e.Endpoint} {e.Status} {e.Ms}ms\");",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Parsed: {entries.Count}, skipped: {candidates.Count - entries.Count}\");",
        "",
        "Entry? TryParseEntry(string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(' ', StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries);",
        "    if (parts is not [var stamp, var ip, var method, var path, var status, var took])",
        "        return null;",
        "    if (method is not (\"GET\" or \"POST\" or \"PUT\" or \"DELETE\"))",
        "        return null;",
        "    if (!DateTime.TryParseExact(stamp, \"yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss\", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, DateTimeStyles.None, out var time))",
        "        return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(status, out var code))",
        "        return null;",
        "    if (!took.EndsWith(\"ms\") || !int.TryParse(took[..^2], out var ms))",
        "        return null;",
        "    return new Entry(time, ip, method, path, code, ms);",
        "}",
        "",
        "record Entry(DateTime Time, string Ip, string Method, string Path, int Status, int Ms)",
        "{",
        "    public string Endpoint => $\"{Method} {Path}\";",
        "}"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "using System.Globalization;",
        "",
        "var lines = new List<string>();",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "    lines.Add(line);",
        "",
        "var candidates = lines.Where(l => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(l)).ToList();",
        "",
        "var entries = candidates",
        "    .Select(TryParseEntry)",
        "    .OfType<Entry>()",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Parsed: {entries.Count}, skipped: {candidates.Count - entries.Count}\");",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine();",
        "Console.WriteLine(\"Status codes:\");",
        "foreach (var (status, count) in entries.CountBy(e => e.Status).OrderBy(p => p.Key))",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"{status}: {count}\");",
        "",
        "var topEndpoints = entries",
        "    .GroupBy(e => e.Endpoint)",
        "    .Select(g => new { Endpoint = g.Key, Hits = g.Count() })",
        "    .OrderByDescending(x => x.Hits)",
        "    .ThenBy(x => x.Endpoint)",
        "    .Take(3);",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine();",
        "Console.WriteLine(\"Top endpoints:\");",
        "foreach (var x in topEndpoints)",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"{x.Endpoint}: {x.Hits}\");",
        "",
        "Entry? TryParseEntry(string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(' ', StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries);",
        "    if (parts is not [var stamp, var ip, var method, var path, var status, var took])",
        "        return null;",
        "    if (method is not (\"GET\" or \"POST\" or \"PUT\" or \"DELETE\"))",
        "        return null;",
        "    if (!DateTime.TryParseExact(stamp, \"yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ss\", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, DateTimeStyles.None, out var time))",
        "        return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(status, out var code))",
        "        return null;",
        "    if (!took.EndsWith(\"ms\") || !int.TryParse(took[..^2], out var ms))",
        "        return null;",
        "    return new Entry(time, ip, method, path, code, ms);",
        "}",
        "",
        "record Entry(DateTime Time, string Ip, string Method, string Path, int Status, int Ms)",
        "{",
        "    public string Endpoint => $\"{Method} {Path}\";",
        "}"
      ],
